{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem","id":1049726,"title":"Immortality and Legacies or Am I a Lich and if so what's your Problem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T00:17:35-08:00","id":1049726,"title":"Immortality and Legacies or Am I a Lich and if so what's your Problem?","content":"I have a hard time wrapping my head around the problem awakened society seems to have with the concept of immortality. I realize that Death is supposed to be a vital part of the CoD, an inevitable end that comes for everyone. And in a certain way that's true, even Archmasters (who don't age iirc) can be killed, allthough it is very hard to do so. Heck even Ascended beings can be dethroned (though I'm less sure wether they can ever be destroyed completly). So death is allways in some form an option. But ageing is something the awakened can handle.... it's just that somehow this seems to be seen as a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Now I can understand why people are upset about the methods employed by the tremere or a bodysnatching mage. Sure. But ghostmages, Morpheans etc don't harm anyone by the virtue of their existence, would they really be considered left handed by definition. Why? Or lets take a look at legacies. Sure the Tremere give them a bad name, but why shouldn't a Life centered Legacy be unable to produce an attainment that prevents aging. There were allready Legacies that slowed it down (Perfect Sovereign in 1e), why not just stop it? That would be what, a perfecting practice of life? Normal spells can be dispelled, but it's very hard to do the same for Legacy attainments. Build a legacy attainment that indefinitly stops your ageing. It probably would be a 4th attainment or so, but you have all your natural lifespan to work toward it. Would such a legacy really be considered left handed? Especially since a legacy around mastering the body like this probably could age again if they wanted to. And doesn't eat souls or babies?<br /> <br /> So what is the problem with an approach to immortality that in of itself doesn't hurt anyone? Does it speak volumes about the fear of death of the practioner? Yeah, maybe. But afaik mages who have other issues aren't declared left handed because of it unless these issues cause serious problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:30:37-08:00","id":1049745,"title":"","content":"For one, I agree with you. However, there is a reason this attitude exists in-setting. If the writers allowed easy immortality, there would be multiple ages-old Mages claiming all the resources and positions of prominence. The game can handle several behind-the-scenes Archmages, but this would be too much. The PCs would be surrounded by a status quo they can barely dent. It's like Vampire: The Masquerade, but much more calcified.<br /> <br /> While Supernal magic should allow agelessness, actually going through it would have harmful ramifications for the game. Note that these aspects can be reconciled. You can assumme that anti-immortality culture of the Pentacle stems from the fact that Mages know its ultimate (political) consequences, and decry it as immoral to feel less petty. Ageless Mages can exist, forced to keep their heads down or face ostracism.<br /> <br /> Final warning. Previous disussions about this subject had a tendency to deteriorate, so tread carefully. People have strong feelings about this, one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:38:49-08:00","id":1049748,"title":"","content":"Even if elder mages achieve immortality of the agelessness &amp; eternal youth type, mages in general have this perpetual and incurable habit of poking in places they <i>really </i>shouldn't be looking in if they want to live a long and healthy life.<br /> <br /> The above is the usual answer I give when faced with questions of where all the ancients are in a setting that facilitates easy immortality. The supernatural world in the CofD is inherently a violent one. Sure, a mage could sit in his favorite couch away from the dangers of the world, but this leads to less hands-on experience and thus a relatively low level of power, so they aren't likely to accumulate enough magical mojo to aim for immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:52:50-08:00","id":1049750,"title":"","content":"None of the big three flavors of ephemeral lich aren't potentially dangerous to have around \u2014 Morpheans steal and keep bits of the Astral in order to learn (or at least poke around a place that can warp cultures as a matter of engineering), ghost-mages are by definition at least ghosts with access to soul-severing magic, and spirit-mages mess with the ecosystems of the Shadow as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Run-of-the-mill agelessness isn't viewed as Left-Handed so much as it is kind of vain \u2014 the aspect of lichdom that typically gets you blacklisted is the extra stuff:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consilia also take action against Left-Handed mages. While the exact definition varies from Consilium to Consilium, a mage is frequently regarded as Left-Handed if her Obsessions or magical practices involve the abuse or destruction of souls, the destruction of the world\u2019s magical potential, routine interference with a Sleeper\u2019s Awakening, the cavalier abuse of Sleepers, Abyssal corruption, contact with the Lower Depths, or <b>the evasion of death by extraordinary and ethically questionable deeds.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:03:35-08:00","id":1049751,"title":"","content":"Ninja'd by Satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-16-2017, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:04:35-08:00","id":1049752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049745#post1049745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, I agree with you. However, there is a reason this attitude exists in-setting. If the writers allowed easy immortality, there would be multiple ages-old Mages claiming all the resources and positions of prominence. The game can handle several behind-the-scenes Archmages, but this would be too much. The PCs would be surrounded by a status quo they can barely dent. It's like Vampire: The Masquerade, but much more calcified.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the design choice made, trying to avoid early edition Ascension prevalence of masters everywhere. I merely aim to understand the in character reasons for this hostile behaviour against life prolonging practices when awakened society flouts alot of social taboos with alarming frequency. I'm not too deeply versed in the Awakening material, but from the impression I've got so far there aren't that many taboos that will lead to a mage being exiled or outright killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> While Supernal magic should allow agelessness, actually going through it would have harmful ramifications for the game. Note that these aspects can be reconciled. You can assumme that anti-immortality culture of the Pentacle stems from the fact that Mages know its ultimate (political) consequences, and decry it as immoral to feel less petty. Ageless Mages can exist, forced to keep their heads down or face ostracism. </div> </div> </div>This explaination seems a bit shaky to me. It assumes alot of forethought and united &quot;idealism&quot; on part of the mage youth I don't really see. In mage society older more experienced mages usually are more powerful, it would make sense for them to push agendas that benefited their own power (such as acceptance of immortality if they are so inclined), convincing younger mages to follow step with political leverage. It's feels a bit like assuming being rich should be banned in todays society as the majority of the population isn't rich and acknowledges that that's bad for them. Instead we tend to aspire to become rich, just as I would assume people would aspire to become immortal.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> <br /> <br /> I can see immortal mages being comparativly less powerful than a more active person of the same age would be. We run into the same problem as vampire here. Elders become lazy and don't develop as many new tricks anymore, but have a vast powerbase upon which they can rest in general. Mages being pushed to persue more dangerous interests by their obsession is certainly a very valid point. That nicely explains why even with the capability of immortality only a few actually live extremly long, except for a few lazy mages who try very hard to abstain from obsessions. But a few would probably exist. Why would these people be social outcasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:13:52-08:00","id":1049754,"title":"","content":"For the same reason archmasters are banned from holding political offices in the Pentacle: They, like liches, are sufficiently removed from the human experience that they look at mages like mages look at Sleepers. Both sects in the Pentacle hate that. For different reasons.<br /> <br /> Remember also that the Diamond had a growing-pang war with itself when one of the Orders (the Tremere) turned out to be soul-eating liches. After a certain point, distrusting mages who prolong their lives is like not being able to call yourself a Socialist and get anywhere in American politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:25:19-08:00","id":1049756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049752#post1049752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would these people be social outcasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaan ninja'd by none other than the developer himself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:30:15-08:00","id":1049757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049754#post1049754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the same reason archmasters are banned from holding political offices in the Pentacle: They, like liches, are sufficiently removed from the human experience that they look at mages like mages look at Sleepers. Both sects in the Pentacle hate that. For different reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't it more the peer pressure of other archmasters that don't want their rivals to control a vast amounts of mages that keeps archmasters out of office? The Silver Ladder itself tries to uplift sleepers, often placing themselves into positions of authority regarding to sleepers. I don't really see their philosophy forbidding an archmaster to do the same with them in order to uplift them. I could see many resenting it, sure, but it fits their goal.<br /> <br /> Good point with the historical context.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <br /> <br /> I suppose that is a fair point. So let's say we redesign the perfect sovereigns (who are probably seen as vain anyway) into a legacy that stays perpetually young through their attainments. Would this cause them to be declared left handed? Depends on the Consilium I suppose, but most would just see it as suspect but not left handed, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:33:05-08:00","id":1049759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049757#post1049757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't it more the peer pressure of other archmasters that don't want their rivals to control a vast amounts of mages that keeps archmasters out of office? The Silver Ladder itself tries to uplift sleepers, often placing themselves into positions of authority regarding to sleepers. I don't really see their philosophy forbidding an archmaster to do the same with them in order to uplift them. I could see many resenting it, sure, but it fits their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters who don't give up political power: Tetrarchs, the Pentacle wouldn't stand for it, too similar to Seer power structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T02:49:27-08:00","id":1049767,"title":"","content":"Archmasters' peer pressure is aimed at not letting them interfere with one another's work using their world-breaking spells, not at turning up to Consilium and saying &quot;you guys are meritocratic, right? Anyone else abe to cast a Dynamic spell? No? I'm in charge&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, the Seer archmages do have command positions in the Pyramid. Other archmasters only go after them for breaking the Pax when they flagrantly cheat on behalf of their Ministry.<br /> <br /> No, the Silver law about the Pentacle's titles having a cap of Master is because of the *well documented and understood* tendency of Imperial wizards to treat everyone else like chesspieces at beat and raw quintessence at worst. After the first few hundred cases of an archmaster putting more priority on their lofty cosmic Obsessions than reality itself, the Pentacle wised up. No one driven enough to seek the Imperial Mysteries is your friend.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder just assumes that any archmage who does have it on her to act as a Sage toward lesser mages will do so by proxy or in disguise of being a master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:10:36-08:00","id":1049813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem#post1049726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I can understand why people are upset about the methods employed by the tremere or a bodysnatching mage. Sure. But ghostmages, Morpheans etc don't harm anyone by the virtue of their existence, would they really be considered left handed by definition. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nnnnot quite right. Ghost Mages are obsessed even by the standards of a splat that has a feature outright called Obsession and aren't really considered a form of immortality anyway; they're static echoes of the Mage they're made from, endlessly repeating forever, and it's Diamond dogma that ghosts thoroughly <i>aren't</i> the same person they were before. The one example we have of a Ghost Mage that retained their personality, soul, and capacity for growth, she turned into a horrifying soul-eating monster.<br /> <br /> Morpheans, meanwhile, are solipsistic non-beings who can only grow by carving pieces of the psyches of others. I don't think that needs explaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:12:34-08:00","id":1049815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049757#post1049757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that is a fair point. So let's say we redesign the perfect sovereigns (who are probably seen as vain anyway) into a legacy that stays perpetually young through their attainments. Would this cause them to be declared left handed? Depends on the Consilium I suppose, but most would just see it as suspect but not left handed, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect that most fairly Wise mages would realize that immortality almost inevitably leads to left-handed behavior. As someone before me noted, the long years slowly remove immortal people from the human experience. There's a reason that the Pure Sovereigns, especially the older ones, are generally arrogant jerks who feel that everyone else is beneath them--and they only live roughly 200 years. After a thousand years, how could any given human really matter all that much to such a being? Sure, liberal applications of Mind effects might solve the problem, but would any mage who chased everlasting life willingly discard its primary benefit--that being the vast perspective that millennia of experience brings?<br /> <br /> As examples, I offer Bayaz and his peers in Joe Abercrombie's <i>First Law</i> trilogy (which I heartily recommend if you haven't read it). If that isn't a fantasy in the mold of the World of Darkness, I don't know what is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:40:13-08:00","id":1049841,"title":"","content":"Ehhh.... the problem with this entire discussion is that &quot;lich&quot; isn't quite the same as &quot;immortal&quot; for a mage. Its trivially easy for a mage to achieve immortality through some Life spells or with some practical use of Death magic. And that's generally acceptable in Mage Society, handwaved away as &quot;not true immortality.&quot; Or &quot;just long lived.&quot; Frankly, I think that's nothing more than lawyer-semantics. Much like the term &quot;Left-Handed&quot; itself, its pretty much a social convention for a mage that went bad-wrong. <br /> <br /> Make no mistake, immortal mages do make interesting antagonists. They also make good advisors if you track them down, and stories are out there with neigh immortal wizards who are benevolant and still very much human in outlook. But, mages being who they are, tend to take things to an extreme. Need a Demesne? Lets hunt down the god of all Foxes, kill it, and take its soul to make one instead of just making a soul stone or two. Obsessions make Monsters out of mages as much as crapping their Nimbus on everyone does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:46:43-08:00","id":1050036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049757#post1049757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that is a fair point. So let's say we redesign the <b>perfect sovereigns (who are probably seen as vain anyway)</b> into a legacy that stays <b>perpetually young</b> through their attainments. Would this cause them to be declared left handed? Depends on the Consilium I suppose, but most would just see it as suspect but not left handed, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the mary-sue levels of boring writing to get behind this would make fanfic.net blush.<br /> <br /> In a fallen world, there's nothing perfect anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T01:04:19-08:00","id":1050358,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's a self-correcting problem. Mages with Obsessions of extending their lifespan, then having an unlimited one ... once they achieve this, would become keenly aware of how killable they are. And this then can go in 2 ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Paranoid defensive measures<br /> In this version the Mage invests ever more effort into not being killable, eventually withdrawing from pretty much everything. There could be a smattering of such Mages around the globe. Fun plotfodder.<br /> <br /> 2) Paranoid offensive measures<br /> This version might be why nobody likes it when the newb Mage goes &quot;maybe I could live a bit longer, right?&quot; Because once they notice how eminently killable they are once functionally ageless, they could turn to paranoia of people trying to kill them. And preventing this preemptively. Meaning they have to be dealt with. The Mage Society at learge would have learned how these things go, and this is why they work to curb the enthusiasm for immortality in younglings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T04:03:52-08:00","id":1050417,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think it's anymore a problem than any other Obsession mages get up to. Which can be pretty nasty, admittedly, but there is nothing that unique about liches that <br /> <br /> The big issue we're dealing with is old, super powerful mages likely far stronger than others in the region, so likely less stop able than a non-long-lived mage. Social rules mean less when no one can enforce them. And history has shown that humans aren't always the most moral of creatures on their own. Being old and powerful isn't unique to liches, but it is fairly common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T04:44:14-08:00","id":1050426,"title":"","content":"Immoral and powerful at least can be salvaged for antagonists. Moral and powerful are far more annoying, because you are gonna keep asking yourself &quot;why my board of powerful and noble masters didn't solve all the problems that I want my players to solve&quot;, like we seen here quite a few times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T05:38:25-08:00","id":1050444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1050426#post1050426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moral and powerful are far more annoying, because you are gonna keep asking yourself &quot;why my board of powerful and noble masters didn't solve all the problems that I want my players to solve&quot;, like we seen here quite a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morality isn't a binary option. A lot of the influence magi have over each other is extracted by doing favours for each other. Even a morally upstanding master has an angle.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's your players mystery. They get nothing from it if the Masters do it for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T06:42:18-08:00","id":1050463,"title":"","content":"Also, lets not forget that, just because someone is engaging in an Awakened taboo, doesn't mean they're not tapped for knowledge. The Mad are sometimes cultivated for their expertise, after all. The big thing we have to ask ourselves is how these guys relate to Mysteries. This has nothing to do with morality and everything to do with Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Seers and Banishers are enemies because these two want to either subvert mysteries for their gods or to destroy them, respectively. Its a war over resources. The Mad create problems for people around them and mess up other Mysteries for the sake of their Obsession-Faults. Reapers eat souls, which are kind of necessary not only for making more mages, but also the souls of mages. They don't kill anyone, they just effectively eat magic, a variation on Banishers. Scelesti work with the Abyss which messes up what kind of magic others can do, threatening mysteries once again.<br /> <br /> So, the question becomes, how do immortal mages threaten Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-17-2017, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:05:40-08:00","id":1050531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1049767#post1049767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmasters' peer pressure is aimed at not letting them interfere with one another's work using their world-breaking spells, not at turning up to Consilium and saying &quot;you guys are meritocratic, right? Anyone else abe to cast a Dynamic spell? No? I'm in charge&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, the Seer archmages do have command positions in the Pyramid. Other archmasters only go after them for breaking the Pax when they flagrantly cheat on behalf of their Ministry.<br /> <br /> No, the Silver law about the Pentacle's titles having a cap of Master is because of the *well documented and understood* tendency of Imperial wizards to treat everyone else like chesspieces at beat and raw quintessence at worst. After the first few hundred cases of an archmaster putting more priority on their lofty cosmic Obsessions than reality itself, the Pentacle wised up. No one driven enough to seek the Imperial Mysteries is your friend.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder just assumes that any archmage who does have it on her to act as a Sage toward lesser mages will do so by proxy or in disguise of being a master.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it hard for the Pentacle to be able to stop an archmaster who wants to rule especially one who's focused in fate or mind. I mean I can understand why they would try to fight it just seems hard to believe they'd remotely succeed without intervention.<br /> <br /> Also, I doubt someone who keeps being ageless would be able to relate with people. That isn't to say they'd be inhuman just like someone who's lived too long to bother with most of the political events. There are life mages who can extend their age for quite a bit but that's quite a lot of focus on just keeping yourself alive longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:24:37-08:00","id":1050539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1050531#post1050531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it hard for the Pentacle to be able to stop an archmaster who wants to rule especially one who's focused in fate or mind. I mean I can understand why they would try to fight it just seems hard to believe they'd remotely succeed without intervention.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible to kill an arch-master and while they're formidable opponents on any level trying to single-handedly maintain control of a restless group of Mages is a losing proposition, or it could just be more trouble than it's worth considering the goal of an arch-master is to Ascend not to lord it over a Consilium. They're totally expected to be there in the background manipulating events there's no stopping that, but openly ruling can be made to be not worth the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:42:04-08:00","id":1057297,"title":"","content":"I agree with the idea that it's pretty easy for a Mage to achieve functional immortality (i.e. Wolverine immortality) in the fact that there is real, currently existing life that is biologically immortal. Just use Life to continue healing your diseases. Just use Life to restore your degrading cells. Just use Mind to keep senility at bay. Of course, make sure you don't accidentally trigger a paradox that results in giving yourself incurable cancer OF THE ABYSS.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Lich, or a Tremere, or whatever, isn't about immortality. It's about reliability. It's about <i>power</i>.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:51:49-08:00","id":1057300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1050531#post1050531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it hard for the Pentacle to be able to stop an archmaster who wants to rule especially one who's focused in fate or mind. I mean I can understand why they would try to fight it just seems hard to believe they'd remotely succeed without intervention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you underestimate the power of a very pissed off Consilium. Archmages are powerful, but discretion is the better part of valor versus trying to claim a hoard of belligerent willworkers, even if you outclass any one of them individually.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:05:39-08:00","id":1057305,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, <i>Geist</i> presents the concept that powerful Ghosts are able to 'stop death' - and by extension, making you alive, because you are not dead - even if they can't quite heal what killed you. That's what makes Sin-Eaters. So a Master of Death could feasibly do this as well, pushing away his own death for decades. Possibly indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:10:05-08:00","id":1057310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057305#post1057305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, <i>Geist</i> presents the concept that powerful Ghosts are able to 'stop death' - and by extension, making you alive, because you are not dead - even if they can't quite heal what killed you. That's what makes Sin-Eaters. So a Master of Death could feasibly do this as well, pushing away his own death for decades. Possibly indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death 2, Shielding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:26:44-08:00","id":1057318,"title":"","content":"The problem with &quot;innocent&quot; immortality is that the outset, it seems perfectly reasonable.<br /> A 20-30-something year old Mage relinquishes control of a powerful indefinite anti-aging spell and rests easy knowing they'll be young and full of vim and vigor until they're killed.<br /> More than enough time to do whatever he wants with his life.<br /> And in many cases, this is exactly what they'll do. They'll pursue their Obsessions, live a full and fruitful life, then dispel their own spell and come to death with open arms.<br /> <br /> However the Pentacle is old, and the wisdom passed down through centuries likely has plenty of horror stories about how the march of centuries warps the perspective of Mages.<br /> Even if their method of immortality is not malicious, the long march of time will likely twist them just as much as the potential for Acts of Hubris does.<br /> And when despite all your magical power you see another, ostensibly similar to you, but who looks at you as if you're an ant, hardly even there, can you trust them?<br /> <br /> So really, the general objection to immortality by most Mages is not overly philosophical, it's practical.<br /> They don't fully trust Mages who seek immortality, because despite all your innocent intentions you could eventually turn into an immortal Madman. Maybe not today, maybe not tomorrow, maybe not ever. It's a possibility, a potential. Something they hope doesn't happen, but know from your interest, that it might.<br /> <br /> Once bitten, twice shy.<br /> And the Pentacle has been bitten a LOT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 03-02-2017, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:03:17-08:00","id":1057341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057305#post1057305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, <i>Geist</i> presents the concept that powerful Ghosts are able to 'stop death' - and by extension, making you alive, because you are not dead - even if they can't quite heal what killed you. That's what makes Sin-Eaters. So a Master of Death could feasibly do this as well, pushing away his own death for decades. Possibly indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. Immortality is actually stupidly easy to get.<br /> <br /> Of course, those kinds of immortality are also stupidly easy to dispel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:10:33-08:00","id":1057345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057341#post1057341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly. Immortality is actually stupidly easy to get.<br /> <br /> Of course, those kinds of immortality are also stupidly easy to dispel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Reliability and power. It's not about the immortality, it's about what you've got to do to make sure you can keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:17:01-08:00","id":1057348,"title":"","content":"Ah, the unholy triangle of Accessibility, Reliability, and Morality/Acceptability. You can get two, but can't get one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:10:59-08:00","id":1057397,"title":"","content":"The question is, if a Mage stops their aging process and someone dispells it, do they &quot;catch up&quot; to their actual age or do they start aging again from that point?<br /> <br /> If the latter, functional immortality is basically a thing since you can just recast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:24:35-08:00","id":1057401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057397#post1057397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, if a Mage stops their aging process and someone dispells it, do they &quot;catch up&quot; to their actual age or do they start aging again from that point?<br /> If the latter, functional immortality is basically a thing since you can just recast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say in the spells themselves, it seems to be the opinion of the devs, (I know I've seen Dave and Rose comment on it) that time would catch up to you. Not sure I agree with that personally, and like I said it's not in the spells or the book, but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:40:09-08:00","id":1057409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057397#post1057397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, if a Mage stops their aging process and someone dispells it, do they &quot;catch up&quot; to their actual age or do they start aging again from that point?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording of Veil of Time makes it reasonably clear that the mage would simply start aging from that point. The <i>real</i> drawback to that spell is that there's no way to spend Experiences while under its effects.<br /> <br /> It also takes a total of 3 Reach to be able to recover from Conditions and Tilts, heal normally, and avoid aging while under the spell's effects--all before spending the 2 reach for indefinite duration. Yes, that's surmountable, but it's non-trivial.<br /> <br /> From the book's text concerning immortal mages, and from the one spell (that I know of) that mentions immunity to aging, it seems that immortality is meant to have some serious baggage attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:32:14-08:00","id":1057447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057341#post1057341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, those kinds of immortality are also stupidly easy to dispel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point, though, that there's a thing about that:<br /> <br /> 2e has made spells a lot easier to dispel, but a lot harder to dispel <i>permanently</i>. Rotes of Dispel Magic are useful but not <i>de rigeur</i>, and the necessary workarounds from not having the Prime to manage Supernal Dispellation means doing like archmages do and proxifying away from your own body can carry you fairly far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:28:02-08:00","id":1057607,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure that there are the odd immortal or at least superhumanly old Mages around in regular Mage politics, but they fake deaths/disguise their nature etc because that's easier than overturning the general idea that Mages have about immortal Mages being heavily involved in things. Same with Archmages. <br /> <br /> I think that there is often a tendency, both in and out of setting, for people to justify things like that as a sort of natural law thing. All mages distrust all immortal Mages inherently! Whereas really it's a case that, in most places in general, the prevailing cultural view of Mage society is that immortal Mages and Archmages involving themselves is seen in a dim light. Whether that's something that is a natural response, or a regressive cultural viewpoint, or a good cultural viewpoint etc is probably debated in setting in the same way we talk about morality in the real world.<br /> <br /> In the latest edition, we're seeing that Mage society is less about the translation of grand cosmic laws, and more like real society, something that comes from somewhere and has an actual history and so on. The Diamond might say their existence is written into the law of reality itself, and maybe it is, but maybe it isn't and they are just cults founded in the ancient world that have survived, albeit changed, like modern religions. <br /> <br /> Immortality is distrusted for cultural reasons, and that's a setting element designed to make the game better to play. Works fine to me. Why do we have the little cultural quirks we do? Because we do, really. You could explore where they came from, but they're not cosmic law. We just have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:46:36-08:00","id":1057655,"title":"","content":"I've always kind of wanted to do a game centred on an immortal Awakened; either one who struck a deal with some Supernal being or Bound, or even an Archmaster, and ended up becoming their agent through the centuries. Particularly fun for an Archmaster, where the person might even be sent back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:09:22-08:00","id":1057700,"title":"","content":"The Changing God is a quite nice inspiration for Immortal Mage, that's for sure. And position of his Castoffs is even more interesting, especially in context of a Mage.<br /> <br /> In Mage, Changing God would be a Mage who uses Life and Fate to create bodies perfect for certain tasks, transforms his almighty self to them, and leaves them behind when done with them. Which, for better or worse, creates a new, blank mental construct which looks a lot like &quot;I have adult abilities and thinking capacity but no memories of me or world around me&quot; amnesia in his place. One that probably would be at least Awakened. Playing one of these in Mage would be...extremely interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:11:18-08:00","id":1057703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057447#post1057447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point, though, that there's a thing about that:<br /> <br /> 2e has made spells a lot easier to dispel, but a lot harder to dispel <i>permanently</i>. Rotes of Dispel Magic are useful but not <i>de rigeur</i>, and the necessary workarounds from not having the Prime to manage Supernal Dispellation means doing like archmages do and proxifying away from your own body can carry you fairly far.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in doubt, praxis it out. Dispelling praxis won't help you jump over &quot;need to know all arcana involved&quot;, but it's a great way to punch through other problems, like Withstand.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:40:55-08:00","id":1059169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1057341#post1057341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly. Immortality is actually stupidly easy to get.<br /> <br /> Of course, those kinds of immortality are also stupidly easy to dispel.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think only the most fantatical Consilia consider life extending spells that can be dispelled to be true Liches. <br /> <br /> I think becoming something extremely inhuman or using monsterious means like Reaping count as true Liches. <br /> <br /> And even for beings like ghost Mages I don't think the punishment is death if they are behaving themselves. More like Exile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:45:52-08:00","id":1059173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059169#post1059169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think only the most fantatical Consilia consider life extending spells that can be dispelled to be true Liches.<br /> <br /> I think becoming something extremely inhuman or using monsterious means like Reaping count as true Liches.<br /> <br /> And even for beings like ghost Mages I don't think the punishment is death if they are behaving themselves. More like Exile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooookay. I didn't realize I was suggesting otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T01:33:40-08:00","id":1059387,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine that Mages that use non-evil means to achieve immortality (like eternal youth Legacy attainments) may not be declared Left Handed, but will still face mounting pressure to give up all influence in Mage politics. For exactly the reasons Dave mentioned, i.e. they are too likely to start treating others as nothing but chess pieces.<br /> <br /> That also makes it kind of a self correcting problem, because a Mage that is no longer part of an Order and Consilium and who had most of her personal friends die of old age doesn't have the necessary protections against all the factions that might want the stuff she hoarded over her longer than normal lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:05:20-08:00","id":1059413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059387#post1059387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to imagine that Mages that use non-evil means to achieve immortality (like eternal youth Legacy attainments) ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I still lack a single example of a possibility in the rules to achieve this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:39:54-08:00","id":1059468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059413#post1059413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still lack a single example of a possibility in the rules to achieve this.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I just mean immortality as in 'not aging', not 'can't be killed'. Just take a spell that prolongs your life, and make it an indefinite duration Legacy Attainment.<br /> Death (or possibly Life) shielding, Veil of Moments, Shapechange, etc.<br /> As your single example, take Veil of Moments as a fifth attainment with the four available Reach spent on Adanced Duration, Indefinite Duration, Ability to regain Willpower, and ability to regain Mana. Just make sure you have Life at three or more, so you have a way to heal.<br /> Though personally I think using Veil of Moments is most boring variant, especially for a fifth Attainment. Much more interesting would be something like a fifth attainment based on Shapechange with Matter added that transforms you into a towering monstrosity of molten metal, with blood of Lava and burning coals as eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:44:03-08:00","id":1059472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059468#post1059468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tto be clear, I just mean immortality as in 'not aging', not 'can't be killed'. Just take a spell that prolongs your life, and make it an indefinite duration Legacy Attainment.<br /> Death (or possibly Life) shielding, Veil of Moments, Shapechange, etc.<br /> As your single example, take Veil of Moments as a fifth attainment with the four available Reach spent on Adanced Duration, Indefinite Duration, Ability to regain Willpower, and ability to regain Mana. Just make sure you have Life at three or more, so you have a way to heal.<br /> Though personally I think using Veil of Moments is most boring variant, especially for a fifth Attainment. Something like a fifth attainment based on Shapechange with Matter added that transforms you into a towering monstrosity of molten metal, with blood of Lava and burning coals as eyes sounds much more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Life/Fate, gain immortality by denying destinys(This works much better using 1e Destiny though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:59:15-08:00","id":1059513,"title":"","content":"I think that if prolonging your lifespan was as easy as a Death Shielding spell, people wouldn't eat souls or become ghost mages or morpheans or whatever. And I don't mean that there are no evil ways to avoid Death, but they have to be a bit more advanced and onerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:01:46-08:00","id":1059515,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Death Shielding spell is in the &quot;It catches up with you if the spell fails&quot; school of immortality methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:05:18-08:00","id":1059519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059468#post1059468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I just mean immortality as in 'not aging', not 'can't be killed'. Just take a spell that prolongs your life, and make it an indefinite duration Legacy Attainment.<br /> Death (or possibly Life) shielding, Veil of Moments, Shapechange, etc.<br /> As your single example, take Veil of Moments as a fifth attainment with the four available Reach spent on Adanced Duration, Indefinite Duration, Ability to regain Willpower, and ability to regain Mana. Just make sure you have Life at three or more, so you have a way to heal.<br /> Though personally I think using Veil of Moments is most boring variant, especially for a fifth Attainment. Much more interesting would be something like a fifth attainment based on Shapechange with Matter added that transforms you into a towering monstrosity of molten metal, with blood of Lava and burning coals as eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, Veil of Moments is afaik the only spell you can do this with and it has some serious disadvantages you didn't mention: you cannot spend experience and neither gain, nor resolve any condition. Which basically means, that you cannot learn anything. So while you might be ageless, you are doomed to never be able to improve your abilities. Kind of a weird thing to do for a mage.<br /> <br /> For transforming into something different, you usually need at least a 4 dot spell of any arcanum, which makes it impossible to get it do indefinite Duration. Besides, beeing a &quot;towering monstrosity of molten metal&quot; is kind of removed from the human experience pretty drastically.<br /> <br /> So I stand by my statement, that I am still waiting for a suitable &quot;easy&quot; way to gain agelessness without either removing yourself strongly from the human experience or extrem disadvantages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:18:22-08:00","id":1059528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059519#post1059519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For transforming into something different, you usually need at least a 4 dot spell of any arcanum, which makes it impossible to get it do indefinite Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>A four dot spell as a fifth Attainment gives you two reach to spend, which is enough for indefinite duration.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059519#post1059519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, beeing a &quot;towering monstrosity of molten metal&quot; is kind of removed from the human experience pretty drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I did that for the 40k joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059519#post1059519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I stand by my statement, that I am still waiting for a suitable &quot;easy&quot; way to gain agelessness without either removing yourself strongly from the human experience or extrem disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>There must be a failure of communication here. In my original post you quoted I explicidly said &quot;non-evil&quot; way, I said nothing about those ways not removing you pretty far from normal human expericen. in fact the rest of my post (which you didn't quote) I directly addressed that as one of the impossible to avoid repercussion of becoming immortal.<br /> <br /> So I stand by my statement that there are non-evil, even easy, ways to become immortal. Mostly because I cannot imagine why you'd ask me for prove that there are ways to become immortal that don't remove one from normal human experience when I already ruled out that this is possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I mean, am I missing something here? I said there are non evil ways to become immortal (with the caveat that they still remove you from normal human experience), to which you say &quot;I still lack a single example of a possibility in the rules to achieve this.&quot;. I then show examples of non-evil ways to become immortal, to which you answer that those don't count because they are ether removing yourself strongly from the human experience or have extrem disadvantages? Well, obviously! I never said they don't remove you from human experience or don't have downsides!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-07-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:20:24-08:00","id":1059529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059519#post1059519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, Veil of Moments is afaik the only spell you can do this with and it has some serious disadvantages you didn't mention: you cannot spend experience and neither gain, nor resolve any condition. Which basically means, that you cannot learn anything. So while you might be ageless, you are doomed to never be able to improve your abilities. Kind of a weird thing to do for a mage.<br /> [snip]<br /> So I stand by my statement, that I am still waiting for a suitable &quot;easy&quot; way to gain agelessness without either removing yourself strongly from the human experience or extrem disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pull all the Reaches needed by Veil of Moments to ignore those disadvantages. Just make sure you're casting it in a Demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:31:19-08:00","id":1059533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059529#post1059529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pull all the Reaches needed by Veil of Moments to ignore those disadvantages. Just make sure you're casting it in a Demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still doesn't let you spend XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:33:03-08:00","id":1059534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059529#post1059529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pull all the Reaches needed by Veil of Moments to ignore those disadvantages. Just make sure you're casting it in a Demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair this is about using Veil of Moments as a indefinite Duration Legacy Attainment, so that it cannot be dispelled. In which case you get a maximum of four Reach that you can spend, of which you need to use to make it indefinite Duration. With only two Reach left you are going to have to make some hard decisions about what you value most: Willpower, Mana, or natural healing. And no spending experience no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:33:00-08:00","id":1059632,"title":"","content":"You could do something like:<br /> <br /> False Reincarnation<br /> (Fate 5, Mind 5)<br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Persuasion, Occult<br /> <br /> Upon death you reincarnate as nearby as possible as a newborn with a Fate to Awaken and regain your memories.<br /> Contact with your Dedicated Tool triggers this Fate.<br /> This spell may only be used on the caster.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The spell's Duration is Lasting.<br /> <br /> Inspired by the &quot;Reborn&quot; from Immortals (page 135) and Cymbeline/Cxaxa Qherephis from Reign of the Exarchs (page 40).<br /> <br /> Heavy on the needed Arcana (two masteries and Gnosis 6). But if you're looking for non-evil, non-inhuman sort-of immortality this might be an option.<br /> It won't come up in a game though. When have you had the time to wait for your reincarnation to mature and awaken in a game? That's one hell of a time-skip.<br /> Still, it might give a character peace of mind knowing death is not the end, only an inconvenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 03-07-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:02:28-08:00","id":1059653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059632#post1059632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do something like:<br /> <br /> False Reincarnation<br /> (Fate 5, Mind 5)<br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Persuasion, Occult<br /> <br /> Upon death you reincarnate as nearby as possible as a newborn with a Fate to Awaken and regain your memories.<br /> Contact with your Dedicated Tool triggers this Fate.<br /> This spell may only be used on the caster.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The spell's Duration is Lasting.<br /> <br /> Inspired by the &quot;Reborn&quot; from Immortals (page 135) and Cymbeline/Cxaxa Qherephis from Reign of the Exarchs (page 40).<br /> <br /> Heavy on the needed Arcana (two masteries and Gnosis 6). But if you're looking for non-evil, non-inhuman sort-of immortality this might be an option.<br /> It won't come up in a game though. When have you had the time to wait for your reincarnation to mature and awaken in a game? That's one hell of a time-skip.<br /> Still, it might give a character peace of mind knowing death is not the end, only an inconvenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, sure, but from the Arcana involved it seems more like your consciousness is fated to possess a child in the womb upon your death. It's not really your soul taking on a new body, because that would probably require Death 2/3 and Life 5 as well (creating a 'virgin birth' of your own new flesh and moving your soul into it as well as your mind.)<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this sounds not only like a possible spell, but also like it may be a secret part of the Esoteric Mysteries of the Guardians of the Veil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:36:56-08:00","id":1059674,"title":"","content":"People point out that life extending spells can be dispelled, but you can also get Mages who melt your head. The problem isn't that the spell can be dispelled, it's that you pissed off someone enough to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:16:36-08:00","id":1059778,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Mages who can or would want to do that are rarer than a naive Obrimos who might unravel the spell just because they saw it and thought &quot;Hey, maybe they're hiding a cool secret under there!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:21:22-08:00","id":1059907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059778#post1059778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Mages who can or would want to do that are rarer than a naive Obrimos who might unravel the spell just because they saw it and thought &amp;quot;Hey, maybe they're hiding a cool secret under there!&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> That not niave Obrimos, that's complete fool of an Obrimos, because even a niave Obrimos is going to use mage sight and try and see what the spell that person cast on themselves does. <br /> <br /> And and a newbie Obrimos would find unraveling the spell hard to do if they could do it at all. <br /> <br /> Also most mages even niave ones will know enough that you don't dispell a spell one someone cast on themselves unless you intend to kill them. It's rude. <br /> <br /> So I find it unlikely compared to someone trying to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:49:17-08:00","id":1059918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059907#post1059907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That not niave Obrimos, that's complete fool of an Obrimos, because even a niave Obrimos is going to use mage sight and try and see what the spell that person cast on themselves does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which <i>costs Willpower</i> and is <i>invasive and rude</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T21:04:51-08:00","id":1059920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059918#post1059918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which <i>costs Willpower</i> and is <i>invasive and rude</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, so it's not exactly a subtle invasion of privacy either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T21:40:52-08:00","id":1059928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059918#post1059918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which <i>costs Willpower</i> and is <i>invasive and rude</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, and dispelling it is not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:17:48-08:00","id":1059939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059928#post1059928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and dispelling it is not?</div> </div> </div> </div>When &quot;Only a complete fool of a mage doesn't pry at another mage's work with the supernatural equivalent of an extended taste-test&quot; is presented as a <i>contrast</i> to &quot;Mages know that for some reason dispelling a mage's spells <i>without</i> intent to murder them is rude,&quot; the problem is not the relative politeness of dispelling an unknown spell as a member of a supernatural species known for probing the limits of advisability and acceptability as they neglect the maintenance of their good sense versus consuming the intimate details of another member of said species's handiwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:22:51-08:00","id":1060190,"title":"","content":"I suppose, but I think it would be rare and that's the kind of Mage who gets themselves killed or worse early on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:24:51-07:00","id":1061488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1059632#post1059632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do something like:<br /> <br /> False Reincarnation<br /> (Fate 5, Mind 5)<br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Persuasion, Occult<br /> <br /> Upon death you reincarnate as nearby as possible as a newborn with a Fate to Awaken and regain your memories.<br /> Contact with your Dedicated Tool triggers this Fate.<br /> This spell may only be used on the caster.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The spell's Duration is Lasting.<br /> <br /> Inspired by the &amp;quot;Reborn&amp;quot; from Immortals (page 135) and Cymbeline/Cxaxa Qherephis from Reign of the Exarchs (page 40).<br /> <br /> Heavy on the needed Arcana (two masteries and Gnosis 6). But if you're looking for non-evil, non-inhuman sort-of immortality this might be an option.<br /> It won't come up in a game though. When have you had the time to wait for your reincarnation to mature and awaken in a game? That's one hell of a time-skip.<br /> Still, it might give a character peace of mind knowing death is not the end, only an inconvenience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Non-evil? Non-inhuman?!? <br /> <br /> This is the god damn textbook definition of Hubris!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T04:25:25-07:00","id":1061505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1061488#post1061488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Non-evil? Non-inhuman?!?<br /> <br /> This is the god damn textbook definition of Hubris!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is pretty much the definition of hubris but I wouldn't really call it <i>evil</i>. It isn't like you're body snatching here, not quite anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T05:05:10-07:00","id":1061511,"title":"","content":"I would argue the devil is in the details. <br /> <br /> If the Mage had the determination to imprint their memories onto the newborn immediately and had to suffer through growth and development all over again then it could be argued that the infant was never really a person and therefore not body snatching.<br /> <br /> But to have a person uniquely different from the Mage who cast the spell grow up with a fate they can't control to awaken and immediately gain the memories of some asshole while retaining their own memories, creating an instant identity crisis and potentially scaring them for life. That...that is just downright evil to me. Because how is that any different from doing that to just some poor random person on the street? Your still robbing someone of the chance for personal Awakening and then brainwashing them to suddenly have all of your memories and desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T05:18:34-07:00","id":1061513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1061511#post1061511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue the devil is in the details.<br /> <br /> If the Mage had the determination to imprint their memories onto the newborn immediately and had to suffer through growth and development all over again then it could be argued that the infant was never really a person and therefore not body snatching.<br /> <br /> But to have a person uniquely different from the Mage who cast the spell grow up with a fate they can't control to awaken and immediately gain the memories of some asshole while retaining their own memories, creating an instant identity crisis and potentially scaring them for life. That...that is just downright evil to me. Because how is that any different from doing that to just some poor random person on the street? Your still robbing someone of the chance for personal Awakening and then brainwashing them to suddenly have all of your memories and desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you said, the devils in the details, and going by the spell, the person was always you. Sure, you didn't know it was you when you were growing up, but as soon as you take hold of your Dedicated Tool you know what's what. Will it be a little shocking? Probably at first, but I don't see it as evil. This isn't some foreign entity taking claim of your mind and you would know it, this was more you regaining something you'd previously lost. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T06:24:53-07:00","id":1061522,"title":"","content":"If that were true then that would be fine (given one was willing to gloss over the implications about conflicting identities and the existential horror of identity.)<br /> <br /> But the spell is called False Reincarnation, not True Reincarnation. If a Mage can truly control how they reincarnate (if they even reincarnate) then is it right for them to decide who they will be in their next life? Especially if that person had dreams and aspirations beyond their past life's own worldly ambitions? And if they can't truly control how they reincarnate without Imperial Practices then what does that say about the life you forever altered just because you feared dying? Because you wanted your ambitions to pass on despite what the people of the future desires for themselves?<br /> <br /> This kind of logic is why Litchs are considered primarily Left-Handed. The desire to persist beyond death is increadably appealing but it's not a path to Wisdom, because on some level it's a deeply selfish one that lends the survival of the self to be superior to all other factors. And pared with a Mage's increadable power and very human flaws it can lead to some truly horrific tragedies. One of which, I will still argue, could be binding a future incarnation to the ghost of a dead Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 03-12-2017, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T06:38:42-07:00","id":1061524,"title":"","content":"This sounds like a good material for a character, PC or NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T07:09:39-07:00","id":1061534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1061522#post1061522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were true then that would be fine (given one was willing to gloss over the implications about conflicting identities and the existential horror of identity.)<br /> <br /> But the spell is called False Reincarnation, not True Reincarnation. If a Mage can truly control how they reincarnate (if they even reincarnate) then is it right for them to decide who they will be in their next life? Especially if that person had dreams and aspirations beyond their past life's own worldly ambitions? And if they can't truly control how they reincarnate without Imperial Practices then what does that say about the life you forever altered just because you feared dying? Because you wanted your ambitions to pass on despite what the people of the future desires for themselves?<br /> <br /> This kind of logic is why Litchs are considered primarily Left-Handed. The desire to persist beyond death is increadably appealing but it's not a path to Wisdom, because on some level it's a deeply selfish one that lends the survival of the self to be superior to all other factors. And pared with a Mage's increadable power and very human flaws it can lead to some truly horrific tragedies. One of which, I will still argue, could be binding a future incarnation to the ghost of a dead Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be called False Reincarnation but there's not really anything false about its effects. It says what it does, and there's nothing wrong with those described effects. If it was meant to be a body snatch then the person who wrote it needs to detail it as such, but as written it's fine. If anything, the spell described should be called Forced Reincarnation. <br /> <br /> And yes, I see no problem with them deciding who they are in their next life. And it isn't like they lose anything from they learned/gained from their new life before regaining their memories anyways. If they have dreams and aspirations before, they'll don't just lose that. They might make an informed decision about whether or not those particular aspirations still mean that much to them but that is normal. People are shaped by their experiences, and just because you suddenly recall experiences that you had previously forgotten doesn't devalue what you experienced before that point. It's like someone who has been stricken with amnesia suddenly remembering everything they had forgotten. Sure, they now have a lot more experience to pull from, but the time that they spent without their memories doesn't go away, it just adds on to who they are.<br /> <br /> Magic generally does what you will it to do, barring paradox. If you can't control how it works without Archmastery and try to make a spell that does it then the spell will fail because you can't do that. If this spell isn't valid it simply won't work, and thus the whole discussion becomes moot. If it does work, then they can control it up to a point and it will work as the spell describes. So either the spell works as detailed, allowing you to reincarnate yourself after death, and use Fate to guide your Dedicated Tool/memories back to you, or the spell doesn't work. It's one or the other, and neither result is inherently evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T13:10:11-07:00","id":1061592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1061524#post1061524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a good material for a character, PC or NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>All things considered, this has been a very fruitful argument. And while I still disagree with the point you're trying to make @Ashenrouge I feel that this may ultimately come down to a difference in philosophy. Which, honestly, like WHW said means this conversation alone will make great fodder for in game character discussions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll rest my belief and reasoning on this: Is anything forced ever really a good thing? Can anyone truly say that they have the right to make the decision for how things should be and follow through with that decision with incredible power &amp; influence when other individual's lives are on the line? Especially when this decision is one born of profound self-interest? I would say that forcing a decision upon another human being can only be a necessary evil, something done when the needs of society or the world are greater and something that should only be done sparingly or out of desperation. Never for a single individual's happiness. Even if that single individual is yourself. <br /> <br /> But then again, I would probably be the Libertine Alchemist if this was an in game conversation. Trying to say that all you're really doing is passing on the Lead Coin to the next generation without their consent rather than paying it to free yourself from worldly suffering and want. That if you really wanted to give your future self the choice to continue on your life's work then why not make a Grimoire or Daimonomicon and just Fate 5 that to eventually be discovered by your future incarnation. Let them wonder and find inspiration form the Wise who blazed a path through the Lie before them. Give them a choice without the burden of a whole other life they never lived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 03-12-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T13:57:33-07:00","id":1061605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049726-immortality-and-legacies-or-am-i-a-lich-and-if-so-what-s-your-problem?p=1061592#post1061592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All things considered, this has been a very fruitful argument. And while I still disagree with the point you're trying to make @Ashenrouge I feel that this may ultimately come down to a difference in philosophy. Which, honestly, like WHW said means this conversation alone will make great fodder for in game character discussions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll rest my belief and reasoning on this: Is anything forced ever really a good thing? Can anyone truly say that they have the right to make the decision for how things should be and follow through with that decision with incredible power &amp; influence when other individual's lives are on the line? Especially when this decision is one born of profound self-interest? I would say that forcing a decision upon another human being can only be a necessary evil, something done when the needs of society or the world are greater and something that should only be done sparingly or out of desperation. Never for a single individual's happiness. Even if that single individual is yourself.<br /> <br /> But then again, I would probably be the Libertine Alchemist if this was an in game conversation. Trying to say that all you're really doing is passing on the Lead Coin to the next generation without their consent rather than paying it to free yourself from worldly suffering and want. That if you really wanted to give your future self the choice to continue on your life's work then why not make a Grimoire or Daimonomicon and just Fate 5 that to eventually be discovered by your future incarnation. Let them wonder and find inspiration form the Wise who blazed a path through the Lie before them. Give them a choice without the burden of a whole other life they never lived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this is one of those things we're just not going to see eye to eye on. I just don't see this as forcing something on someone else. You've made the conscious decision to force your own rebirth. The person who will inherit your memories isn't some stranger, it's still just you, albeit a you who has forgotten he made that choice. I can see why you might come to your conclusion it's just not one I agree with. That said, this goes to show how Acts of Hubris might get out of hand when one party sees something as totally evil while another party sees it as perfectly justifiable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}